Every Gigabyte — credits and third-party material

Picture
- Drawn entirely in code (SVG rendered frame by frame in headless Chromium).
- lib.js is adapted from the Assembly-Line Diagram demo of Lemo-Opuscar
  (https://github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar), MIT licence. The style itself (STYLE.md) is from the same library.
- The look (blue sardines with big eyes, navy tin, cream) follows the Sardeenz logo,
  assets/sardeenz-src.svg in https://github.com/rh-aiservices-bu/sardeenz; a copy is in look/sardeenz-logo.svg.
- Render, mux and sound-effect tools: Lemo-Opuscar core/, MIT licence.

Fonts (subsets in fonts/, SIL Open Font License 1.1)
- Big Shoulders Display — Patric King / The Big Shoulders Project Authors. https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Big+Shoulders+Display
- Archivo — Omnibus-Type / The Archivo Project Authors. https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Archivo

Voice
- Synthetic narration: Kokoro-82M text-to-speech (Apache-2.0), voice "bm_george", run offline through kokoro-onnx (MIT).

Music and sound effects
- Original score and all sound effects synthesized in mix.py (numpy / scipy). No samples or recordings.

Names
- MIG, Kubernetes and Redis are named as the technologies the film explains; they are trademarks of their owners
  (NVIDIA Corporation, The Linux Foundation, Redis Ltd.). No logos are shown.
